1
00:00:00,440 --> 00:00:03,159
Hi,  and  welcome  back  to  act.  You

2
00:00:03,159 --> 00:00:05,040
already  have  a  clearer  solution

3
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:06,720
from  the  last  unit.  Now  the

4
00:00:06,720 --> 00:00:08,679
question  changes.  How  would  that

5
00:00:08,679 --> 00:00:10,320
solution  become  something  you  could

6
00:00:10,320 --> 00:00:12,880
actually  carry  out?  A  good  idea

7
00:00:12,880 --> 00:00:15,679
is  not  yet  a  plan.  Planning  means

8
00:00:15,679 --> 00:00:18,320
turning  the  idea  into  clear  work.

9
00:00:18,320 --> 00:00:19,880
What  needs  to  happen,  in  what

10
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:22,240
order,  what  each  step  needs,  and

11
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:23,720
when  it  should  be  done?

12
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:25,439
The  goal  is  not  to  make  the  plan

13
00:00:25,439 --> 00:00:27,560
complicated.  The  goal  is  to  make

14
00:00:27,560 --> 00:00:29,791
the  next  action  obvious.

15
00:00:30,111 --> 00:00:31,711
One  of  the  easiest  planning

16
00:00:31,711 --> 00:00:33,470
mistakes  is  keeping  the  project

17
00:00:33,470 --> 00:00:35,791
too  big  in  your  head.  Run  and

18
00:00:35,791 --> 00:00:38,151
awareness  initiative  sounds  clear,

19
00:00:38,151 --> 00:00:40,191
but  it  is  still  too  large  to  act

20
00:00:40,191 --> 00:00:41,151
on.

21
00:00:41,151 --> 00:00:43,111
A  useful  plan  breaks  a  project

22
00:00:43,111 --> 00:00:45,390
into  main  parts,  then  breaks  each

23
00:00:45,390 --> 00:00:47,671
part  into  smaller  tasks.

24
00:00:47,671 --> 00:00:49,351
Think  of  it  like  opening  a  box

25
00:00:49,351 --> 00:00:51,351
and  finding  smaller  boxes  inside

26
00:00:51,351 --> 00:00:53,871
it.  The  project  is  the  big  box.

27
00:00:53,871 --> 00:00:55,351
The  main  steps  are  the  smaller

28
00:00:55,351 --> 00:00:57,910
boxes.  The  tasks  inside  them  are

29
00:00:57,910 --> 00:00:59,150
the  pieces  of  work  you  can

30
00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:00,332
actually  do.  too.

31
00:01:00,612 --> 00:01:02,452
Imagine  the  solution  is  to  run

32
00:01:02,452 --> 00:01:04,211
three  awareness  sessions  for  high

33
00:01:04,211 --> 00:01:06,492
school  students.  One  main  step

34
00:01:06,492 --> 00:01:09,092
could  be  prepare  the  content.  That

35
00:01:09,092 --> 00:01:11,091
can  become  smaller  tasks.  Collect

36
00:01:11,091 --> 00:01:12,931
reliable  information,  choose  the

37
00:01:12,931 --> 00:01:15,532
key  messages,  prepare  simple  slides

38
00:01:15,532 --> 00:01:17,332
and  check  the  materials.

39
00:01:17,332 --> 00:01:19,611
Another  main  step  could  be  arrange

40
00:01:19,611 --> 00:01:21,332
the  session,  which  may  include

41
00:01:21,332 --> 00:01:23,252
finding  a  suitable  place,  checking

42
00:01:23,252 --> 00:01:25,412
permission,  choosing  a  time  and

43
00:01:25,412 --> 00:01:26,771
preparing  what  the  participants

44
00:01:26,771 --> 00:01:27,972
need.

45
00:01:27,972 --> 00:01:29,892
Once  the  work  becomes  smaller,  it

46
00:01:29,892 --> 00:01:31,292
becomes  easier  to  see  what  is

47
00:01:31,292 --> 00:01:31,998
missing.

48
00:01:31,998 --> 00:01:34,558
A  practical  plan  usually  answers  a

49
00:01:34,558 --> 00:01:36,438
few  simple  questions.

50
00:01:36,438 --> 00:01:38,277
What  needs  to  be  done?  What

51
00:01:38,277 --> 00:01:40,198
resources  are  needed?  What  will

52
00:01:40,198 --> 00:01:42,438
those  resources  cost?  Who  is

53
00:01:42,438 --> 00:01:44,438
responsible  for  doing  or  supporting

54
00:01:44,438 --> 00:01:46,877
the  task?  When  should  it  happen

55
00:01:46,877 --> 00:01:48,878
and  where  should  it  happen?

56
00:01:48,878 --> 00:01:50,838
These  questions  connect  the  idea

57
00:01:50,838 --> 00:01:52,958
to  reality.  If  one  of  them  is

58
00:01:52,958 --> 00:01:54,958
missing,  the  plan  may  still  look

59
00:01:54,958 --> 00:01:57,158
good  on  paper,  but  execution  can

60
00:01:57,158 --> 00:01:58,748
become  difficult  later.

61
00:01:59,028 --> 00:02:01,748
Resources  are  not  only  money.

62
00:02:01,748 --> 00:02:03,708
A  resource  can  be  a  room,  a

63
00:02:03,708 --> 00:02:07,148
laptop,  printed  material,  transport,

64
00:02:07,148 --> 00:02:09,788
a  contact  person,  information,  or

65
00:02:09,788 --> 00:02:11,188
time.

66
00:02:11,188 --> 00:02:13,068
Cost  means  checking  what  those

67
00:02:13,068 --> 00:02:15,388
resources  may  require  financially

68
00:02:15,388 --> 00:02:16,828
instead  of  discovering  it  too

69
00:02:16,828 --> 00:02:18,068
late.

70
00:02:18,068 --> 00:02:20,628
For  each  task,  ask,  "What  do  I

71
00:02:20,628 --> 00:02:22,508
need  for  this  to  happen?"

72
00:02:22,508 --> 00:02:25,027
Then,  ask,  "Do  I  already  have  it?

73
00:02:25,027 --> 00:02:27,148
Can  I  access  it?  Or  would  I  need

74
00:02:27,148 --> 00:02:28,787
another  option?"

75
00:02:28,787 --> 00:02:30,347
This  simple  check  can  reveal

76
00:02:30,347 --> 00:02:31,868
problems  before  they  become

77
00:02:31,868 --> 00:02:33,664
expensive  or  stressful.

78
00:02:33,664 --> 00:02:36,024
Time  and  place  also  shape  the

79
00:02:36,024 --> 00:02:38,503
plan.  A  task  may  be  simple,  but

80
00:02:38,503 --> 00:02:40,503
still  fail  if  it  is  scheduled  too

81
00:02:40,503 --> 00:02:42,824
late  or  in  the  wrong  place.  So,

82
00:02:42,824 --> 00:02:45,423
give  important  tasks  a  realistic

83
00:02:45,423 --> 00:02:47,383
time  and  think  about  which  tasks

84
00:02:47,383 --> 00:02:49,824
must  happen  before  others.

85
00:02:49,824 --> 00:02:51,863
Then  check  the  location.  Is  it

86
00:02:51,863 --> 00:02:53,584
suitable  for  the  people  involved?

87
00:02:53,584 --> 00:02:55,544
Is  it  available?  Does  it  support

88
00:02:55,544 --> 00:02:57,464
what  the  activity  needs?

89
00:02:57,464 --> 00:02:59,744
Planning  is  not  guessing  a  perfect

90
00:02:59,744 --> 00:03:01,664
future.  It  is  making  reasonable

91
00:03:01,664 --> 00:03:04,122
decisions  before  action  starts.

92
00:03:04,122 --> 00:03:06,162
Here's  a  quick  way  to  test  the

93
00:03:06,162 --> 00:03:08,881
idea.  Take  one  main  step  from  a

94
00:03:08,881 --> 00:03:10,842
sample  initiative  and  ask  six

95
00:03:10,842 --> 00:03:12,122
questions.

96
00:03:12,122 --> 00:03:14,202
What  are  the  smaller  tasks?

97
00:03:14,202 --> 00:03:16,322
What  resources  are  needed?

98
00:03:16,322 --> 00:03:18,402
What  may  cost  money?

99
00:03:18,402 --> 00:03:20,122
Who  needs  to  handle  or  support

100
00:03:20,122 --> 00:03:21,082
it?

101
00:03:21,082 --> 00:03:23,122
When  should  it  happen?  And  where

102
00:03:23,122 --> 00:03:25,641
should  it  happen?

103
00:03:25,641 --> 00:03:27,042
You  do  not  need  to  complete  a

104
00:03:27,042 --> 00:03:29,321
full  project  plan  now.

105
00:03:29,321 --> 00:03:31,122
The  point  is  to  notice  how  much

106
00:03:31,122 --> 00:03:33,481
clearer  an  idea  becomes  when  you

107
00:03:33,481 --> 00:03:35,602
move  from  a  broad  intention  to

108
00:03:35,602 --> 00:03:36,872
specific  work.

109
00:03:36,872 --> 00:03:40,192
So,  the  main  idea  is  simple.

110
00:03:40,192 --> 00:03:42,872
Planning  turns  a  solution  into

111
00:03:42,872 --> 00:03:44,751
manageable  work.

112
00:03:44,751 --> 00:03:47,352
Break  the  project  into  main  steps,

113
00:03:47,352 --> 00:03:50,072
break  those  steps  into  tasks,  then

114
00:03:50,072 --> 00:03:52,792
connect  each  task  to  resources,

115
00:03:52,792 --> 00:03:56,032
cost,  responsibility,  time,  and

116
00:03:56,032 --> 00:03:57,552
place.

117
00:03:57,552 --> 00:03:59,432
In  the  next  lesson,  we  will  look

118
00:03:59,432 --> 00:04:01,872
at  the  next  problem.  A  plan  can

119
00:04:01,872 --> 00:04:05,071
be  complete  and  still  be  weak.  We

120
00:04:05,071 --> 00:04:06,911
will  learn  how  to  check  it,  find

121
00:04:06,911 --> 00:04:08,872
Understand  unrealistic  assumptions

122
00:04:08,872 --> 00:04:10,872
and  improve  it  before  action

123
00:04:10,872 --> 00:04:12,111
begins.

124
00:04:12,111 --> 00:04:13,832
That's  it  for  today  and  I'll  see

125
00:04:13,832 --> 00:04:15,413
you  in  the  next  lesson.

